  "answer": "IMF staff recommends that the BSP consider moving towards a positive neutral level for the countercyclical capital buffer (CCyB) to help preempt the build-up of vulnerabilities and maintain releasable buffers when risks materialize. For commercial real estate exposures, staff recommends replacing the cap with a sectoral systemic risk buffer. This reform would help capture broader risks in the real estate sector and provide banks with price-based incentives to align their loan portfolios and capital buffers with systemic risk, provided implementation ensures there are no unintended changes in the macroprudential stance.",
